hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1266","Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Durhami and Al-Hussein bin Issa Al-Bistami narrated to us, saying: Anas bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying on his camel, heading to Tabuk."
"1267","Bundar, narrated to us Yahya, narrated to us Abd al-Malik, who is Ibn Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he was “praying on his mount, heading from Mecca, and it descended: Wherever you turn, there is the face of God.”"
